In article <1992Mar11.224006.21703@beaver.cs.washington.edu> pullen@cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:
>In article <JOHNSON.92Mar11114131@physics.berkeley.edu> johnson@physics.berkeley.edu writes:
>>A quick question:  How can i get the most stones (rocks) per wish?
>>The best i have come up with so far is to wish for 3 cursed scrolls of
>>genocide, genocide stone golems, and then smash them.  Any better
>>ideas?
>Take it from a poly piler: Wish for 3 cursed scrolls of genocide, and
>send in Umber Hulks instead. Don't kill them, but rather let them run
>around through the walls on the level resulting in dozens of boulders
>and several thousand rocks. Use a pick-axe to break the boulders and
>you can even dig pits in the ground to "recycle" the Umber Hulks
>because they will fall down to the next level and you can get another
>5K rocks or so there too, and so on. Much more efficient use of a wish.

Very true, very true....When we over here at spoiler central were trying to
figure out ways to get rocks, we found that a cursed scroll of genocide is
perhaps the most useful item in the game.  But, try this for size...

We found that the problem with Umber Hulk clouds is that they take a long time
to cover the whole floor...Soooooooo..
we tamed one and slipped a leash over his neck...then we lead him to where
they had not reached yet and increased his usefulness 10-fold...

There is one HUGE advantage to cursed genociding stone golems, though.  I
found that about 1/2 of them contained spellbooks (this is NOT from the source
code, just experience...I may have been lucky).  In this way (using a lot of
scrolls) I got about 70 spellbooks, and had identify read about 10 times...
Putting them in a poly-pile will get you all of the variety you need...

